	(text "DESIGN NOTES (summary; full analysis in docs/stage2/sheet6-design-notes.md)\n1. LEDs: READY = FPGA pin 65 (off: blank/configuring/reset/not armed; ~1.5 Hz blink: armed, not configured; steady: configured;\n   ~12 Hz blink: watchdog flag). RP0 link, RP1 heartbeat, RP2 mailbox/IRQ, RP3 fault (FW-9..FW-12): off whenever the RP2040,\n   the X4 or the carrier is off. +3V3 LED: carrier logic power. X4 LED: X4 12 V rail live from ANY source - INDICATOR ONLY.\n2. SW601 ON = active: 1 512 KB mode, 2 INT6, 3 disable, 4 RP2040 JTAG option. All OFF = 64 KB, INT2, armed, JTAG isolated.\n   1-3 are sampled only during a Zorro reset (STATUS b4-b6 show them live). 4 acts immediately. Change with the A2000 off.\n3. SW601-4 ON ONLY WITH NO CABLE ON J201. If both drive JTAG, U403's 330R resistors (sheet 4) limit the current to 10.9 mA.\n4. J601 debug header through U601 (Ioff, VCC isolation): no path into the FPGA when it is erased, configuring or unpowered.\n   Pin 1 is a protected output (PTC + Schottky): a tool cannot back-feed the carrier. Default: DBG0-2 in, DBG3 out (straps).\n5. Not yet validated: an ERC-clean result does not imply electrical correctness. No PCB manufacture authorised."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
